/40 bg-deep/90 text-green shadow-[0_0_25px_rgba(34,197,94,0.25)] backdrop-blur-md transition-all hover:bg-green hover:text-deep\"><span class=\"pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 rounded-full bg-green/20 blur-md animate-breathe\"></span><svg class=\"relative h-6 w-6\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M17.472 14.382c-.297-.149-1.758-.867-2.03-.967-.273-.099-.471-.148-.67.15-.197.297-.767.966-.94 1.164-.173.199-.347.223-.644.075-.297-.15-1.255-.463-2.39-1.475-.883-.788-1.48-1.761-1.653-2.059-.173-.297-.018-.458.13-.606.134-.133.298-.347.446-.52.149-.174.198-.298.298-.497.099-.198.05-.371-.025-.52-.075-.149-.669-1.612-.916-2.207-.242-.579-.487-.5-.669-.51-.173-.008-.371-.01-.57-.01-.198 0-.52.074-.792.372-.272.297-1.04 1.016-1.04 2.479 0 1.462 1.065 2.875 1.213 3.074.149.198 2.096 3.2 5.077 4.487.709.306 1.262.489 1.694.625.712.227 1.36.195 1.871.118.571-.085 1.758-.719 2.006-1.413.248-.694.248-1.289.173-1.413-.074-.124-.272-.198-.57-.347m-5.421 7.403h-.004a9.87 9.87 0 01-5.031-1.378l-.361-.214-3.741.982.998-3.648-.235-.374a9.86 9.86 0 01-1.51-5.26c.001-5.45 4.436-9.884 9.888-9.884 2.64 0 5.122 1.03 6.988 2.898a9.825 9.825 0 012.893 6.994c-.003 5.45-4.437 9.884-9.885 9.884m8.413-18.297A11.815 11.815 0 0012.05 0C5.495 0 .16 5.335.157 11.892c0 2.096.547 4.142 1.588 5.945L.057 24l6.305-1.654a11.882 11.882 0 005.683 1.448h.005c6.554 0 11.89-5.335 11.893-11.893a11.821 11.821 0 00-3.48-8.413Z\"></path></svg></button></div><main class=\"pt-28 md:pt-32\"><article class=\"px-6 py-16 md:px-16 md:py-24\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-3xl\"><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-muted\"><span class=\"text-green\">Network &amp; Infrastructure</span><time dateTime=\"2026-08-17\">2026-08-17</time></div><h1 class=\"mt-6 font-serif font-semibold leading-[1.1] text-[clamp(2rem,5vw,3.75rem)]\">The Network That Worked Until It Didn&#x27;t</h1><figure class=\"mt-12\"><div class=\"relative flex justify-center\"><div class=\"absolute -inset-4 bg-green/[0.06] blur-2xl\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/dzyxm0rhg/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1786859643/frayed-cable-bundle_whifkh.png\" alt=\"The Network That Worked Until It Didn&#x27;t\" class=\"relative w-full max-w-sm border border-ink/20 shadow-[0_24px_70px_rgba(0,0,0,0.55)]\"/></div><figcaption class=\"mt-5 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-muted\">Fig. 01 — The frayed cable bundle.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"journal-body mt-14\"><p>The call came during a school day.</p>\n<p>Students were trying to access online resources. Several computers had already lost connectivity. Staff couldn't tell where the fault was, only that parts of the network kept disappearing.</p>\n<p>The network had not failed overnight.</p>\n<p>It had been failing slowly for years.</p>\n<h2>What we found</h2>\n<p>Walking through the campus, the first issue was visible before opening a single cabinet.</p>\n<p>A section of the network linking school buildings had been installed using <strong>indoor Ethernet cable on an outdoor run</strong>. Years of sun exposure had hardened and damaged the cable jacket. The link was no longer reliable.</p>\n<p>Inside the buildings, the story continued.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>No patch panels.</li>\n<li>No structured cable management.</li>\n<li>No proper trunking in several runs.</li>\n<li>Multiple unmanaged switches distributed across the network.</li>\n<li>Little visibility into where cables started or ended.</li>\n<li>Several computers disconnected or improperly terminated.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Nothing looked catastrophic in isolation.</p>\n<p>Together, however, every future fault became harder to find, harder to diagnose and more disruptive to learning.</p>\n<h2>The real problem</h2>\n<p>The damaged outdoor cable was only the symptom.</p>\n<p>The larger issue was that the network had grown without structure.</p>\n<p>New devices had been added whenever they were needed. Additional cables had been pulled whenever someone needed another connection. Small decisions accumulated over time until nobody had a clear view of the entire network.</p>\n<p>When something stopped working, troubleshooting became a process of elimination rather than a process of management.</p>\n<h2>Why this matters</h2>\n<p>Schools depend on connectivity far more than they did a decade ago.</p>\n<p>Student portals, administration systems, online learning resources, examinations, printers and communication platforms all rely on the same infrastructure.</p>\n<p>When the network becomes unreliable, teaching time is lost, administrative work slows down and students feel the impact immediately.</p>\n<h2>The work</h2>\n<p>The damaged runs were identified and replaced with proper outdoor-rated cable where required.</p>\n<p>Existing cable routes were reorganised and properly terminated.</p>\n<p>Network points that had lost connectivity were tested and restored.</p>\n<p>Computers that could not access the network were traced, diagnosed and brought back online.</p>\n<p>The goal was not to add complexity.</p>\n<p>The goal was to restore reliability and create a network that staff could depend on every day.</p>\n<h2>The lesson</h2>\n<p>Most network failures are not caused by a single dramatic event.</p>\n<p>They come from years of shortcuts.</p>\n<p>The wrong cable in the wrong environment.\nThe missing labels.\nThe unmanaged growth.\nThe assumption that if it works today, it will work tomorrow.</p>\n<p>Eventually those shortcuts become the outage.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>If your organisation relies on a network that nobody fully understands, the problem is rarely the latest fault.</p>\n<p>The problem is usually the system underneath it.</p>\n</div><div class=\"mt-16 border-t border-ink/10 pt-10\"><a href=\"https://wa.me/254736194051?text=Hi%20Sonny,%20I%20just%20read%20the%20journal.%20I%20think%20my%20business%20has%20a%20systems%20problem.\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"group inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-ink/30 pb-1 text-sm uppercase tracking-widest transition-colors hover:border-green hover:text-green\">Begin the diagnostic<svg width=\"11\" height=\"11\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\" fill=\"none\" class=\"transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1 group-hover:-translate-y-1\"><path d=\"M2 10L10 2M10 2H4M10 2V8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"></path></svg></a></div><a class=\"mt-10 inline-block text-sm text-muted transition-colors hover:text-ink\" href=\"/journal\">← All field reports</a></div></article></main><!--$--><!--/$--><script id=\"_R_\">(globalThis[\"TURBOPACK\"] || (globalThis[\"TURBOPACK\"] = [])).push({\"otherChunks\":[\"static/chunks/1pcw6gskne7pf.js\",\"static/chunks/0vm8zo6v48m9c.js\",\"static/chunks/2-liacn1-fmrj.js\",\"static/chunks/3ncqdelv46e8a.js\"],\"runtimeModuleIds\":[94553]});</script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/1pcw6gskne7pf.js\" async=\"\"></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1:\\\"$Sreact.fragment\\\"\\n2:\\\"/_next/static/chunks/3qfy96eoyh-ek.js\\\"\\n3:\\\"/_next/static/chunks/1_q4oc079m3pu.js\\\"\\n4:I[84834,[\\\"$2\\\",\\\"$3\\\"],\\\"default\\\"]\\n5:I[88115,[\\\"$2\\\",\\\"$3\\\"],\\\"default\\\"]\\n6:I[39756,[\\\"$2\\\",\\\"$3\\\"],\\\"default\\\"]\\n7:I[37457,[\\\"$2\\\",\\\"$3\\\"],\\\"default\\\"]\\nd:I[97367,[\\\"$2\\\",\\\"$3\\\"],\\\"OutletBoundary\\\"]\\ne:\\\"$Sreact.suspense\\\"\\n10:\\\"ViewportBoundary\\\"\\n11:I[97367,[\\\"$2\\\",\\\"$3\\\"],\\\"$10\\\"]\\n13:\\\"MetadataBoundary\\\"\\n14:I[97367,[\\\"$2\\\",\\\"$3\\\"],\\\"$13\\\"]\\n16:I[68027,[\\\"$2\\\",\\\"$3\\\"],\\\"default\\\",1]\\n:HL[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/1pw566iu1r5qg.css\\\",\\\"style\\\"]\\n:HL[\\\"/_next/static/media/068444135650a82f-s.p.24u93d7s5mbjp.woff2\\\",\\\"font\\\",{\\\"crossOrigin\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"font/woff2\\\"}]\\n:HL[\\\"/_next/static/media/07c7676b89ed2778-s.p.2bn3s6zvc0dyp.w