l runs.</li>\n<li>Multiple unmanaged switches distributed across the network.</li>\n<li>Little visibility into where cables started or ended.</li>\n<li>Several computers disconnected or improperly terminated.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Nothing looked catastrophic in isolation.</p>\n<p>Together, however, every future fault became harder to find, harder to diagnose and more disruptive to learning.</p>\n<h2>The real problem</h2>\n<p>The damaged outdoor cable was only the symptom.</p>\n<p>The larger issue was that the network had grown without structure.</p>\n<p>New devices had been added whenever they were needed. Additional cables had been pulled whenever someone needed another connection. Small decisions accumulated over time until nobody had a clear view of the entire network.</p>\n<p>When something stopped working, troubleshooting became a process of elimination rather than a process of management.</p>\n<h2>Why this matters</h2>\n<p>Schools depend on connectivity far more than they did a decade ago.</p>\n<p>Student portals, administration systems, online learning resources, examinations, printers and communication platforms all rely on the same infrastructure.</p>\n<p>When the network becomes unreliable, teaching time is lost, administrative work slows down and students feel the impact immediately.</p>\n<h2>The work</h2>\n<p>The damaged runs were identified and replaced with proper outdoor-rated cable where required.</p>\n<p>Existing cable routes were reorganised and properly terminated.</p>\n<p>Network points that had lost connectivity were tested and restored.</p>\n<p>Computers that could not access the network were traced, diagnosed and brought back online.</p>\n<p>The goal was not to add complexity.</p>\n<p>The goal was to restore reliability and create a network that staff could depend on every day.</p>\n<h2>The lesson</h2>\n<p>Most network failures are not caused by a single dramatic event.</p>\n<p>They come from years of shortcuts.</p>\n<p>The wrong cable in the wrong environment.\nThe missing labels.\nThe unmanaged growth.\nThe assumption that if it works today, it will work tomorrow.</p>\n<p>Eventually those shortcuts become the outage.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>If your organisation relies on a network that nobody fully understands, the problem is rarely the latest fault.</p>\n<p>The problem is usually the system underneath it.</p>\nf:[[\"children\",{\"s\":\"__PAGE__\",\"h\":160,\"d\":{\"r\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"main\",null,{\"className\":\"pt-28 md:pt-32\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"px-6 py-16 md:px-16 md:py-24\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto max-w-3xl\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline justify-between font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-muted\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-green\",\"children\":\"Network & Infrastructure\"}],[\"$\",\"time\",null,{\"dateTime\":\"2026-08-17\",\"children\":\"2026-08-17\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-6 font-serif font-semibold leading-[1.1] text-[clamp(2rem,5vw,3.75rem)]\",\"children\":\"The Network That Worked Until It Didn't\"}],[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative flex justify-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute -inset-4 bg-green/[0.06] blur-2xl\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://res.cloudinary.com/dzyxm0rhg/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1786859643/frayed-cable-bundle_whifkh.png\",\"alt\":\"The Network That Worked Until It Didn't\",\"className\":\"relative w-full max-w-sm border border-ink/20 shadow-[0_24px_70px_rgba(0,0,0,0.55)]\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"figcaption\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-muted\",\"children\":\"Fig. 01 — The frayed cable bundle.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"journal-body mt-14\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":